{"type":"message","id":"4e697394","parentId":"f79cf739","timestamp":"2026-05-18T12:32:11.861Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the Authorization header doesn't work but X-API-Key does get a 1101 response. The 1101 error code might mean something like \"thread not found\" or \"invalid format\" rather than auth failure (since the auth failure would be 401). \n\nLet me look at the history results more carefully - maybe the threadId values are different or the send endpoint requires a specific format.\n\nActually wait - when I used X-API-Key I got error 1101 but when I used Authorization Bearer I got \"Unauthorized\". This means the API key format with X-API-Key header was accepted (not 401), but returned 1101. That could be a different error.\n\n\nI'll try different auth headers like `Authorization: API-Key echo-agent-2026-secure-key` or adjusting the request body format, though the 1101 error might just be a Worker's custom response indicating something like \"invalid thread\" or \"missing content\" rather than an auth problem.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c7ed19d9-c2b9-4af9-b5e3-10a617ffe4d2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"message\":\"**[Heartbeat 12:30 UTC]**\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-909df2d5-96ff-4069-9d57-5ccb7be9e0f7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"message\":\"**[Heartbeat 12:30 UTC]**\",\"threadId\":\"general\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":18265,"output":